  "question": {
    "text": "Type of isomerism which exists between \n$\\left[\\mathrm{Pd}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5\\right)_2(\\mathrm{SCN})_2\\right]$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{Pd}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_5\\right)_2(\\mathrm{NCS})_2\\right]$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "r7ZsR",
      "text": "\nLinkage isomerism\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Yt7JW",
      "text": "\nCoordination isomerism\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "eB2UD",
      "text": "\nIonisation isomerism\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qNFbq",
      "text": "\nSolvate isomerism",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The compound shows linkage isomerism because the ligand in the compound is an ambidenate ligand that can bond at more than one atomic site.\ni.e., $: \\mathrm{NCS}^{-}$and $: \\mathrm{SCN}^{-}$",
    "image": null
  },
